From c0cdd140b480532d9af215d24c036a3272a3d725 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:09:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] port 1b9247b1 1ce30723: serve: --batch runs an image
 request alone; a dead encoder fails only image requests; log which messages
 carry the pictures of an image request

v0.2.12 still keeps one M-RoPE table per device and its server sends BGENI straight into batch slots, so an image
decoding beside other slots corrupts their rows (#1242). generate_batched hands a request with embeddings to
_generate_alone when the engine does not say INFO mrope_slots=1 (image_alone(), the server half of 77e9b9e1): it
queues behind earlier image requests (image_line), new requests stand back from its arrival (not counted as
waiting, so a read that gave way still gets the control lines - no deadlock), the slots decode to their end, then
it takes the control lines with every slot free and runs GENI on the solo path to its DONE.
- STRATA_IMAGE_WAIT_S (120): an image that waited longer for the slots gives up with a 503 the client can retry
  (ImageWaitTimeout, a GpuBusy), and the text held behind it goes on.
- An engine refusal ("ERR vision: ...") waits for the slots again (up to 3 tries) instead of failing.
- A dead or unstartable vision encoder no longer fails text-only requests (load(vision=False) for generation; the
  encoder is started for image requests and tool pictures only).
- 1ce30723: one line per image request saying which messages carry its pictures.
Text-only traffic sends the same lines as before.

Adaptations to v0.2.12:
- _take_control keeps upstream's entry [plen, arrival, new, prompt, request], the queue deadline, the #4738
  re-check and the leave-notify; the image gate adds `quiet` (the image request itself), the stand-back of `new`
  requests, and the `standing` count from 3850a79e (load_counts now reports standing / image_line, the
  test_load image cases of 3850a79e come back). STRATA_ADMIT_SHORT_FIRST orders only `counted` entries (the
  condition our ADMIT_SHORT_FIRST copy had, plan F13), and the #4738 re-check uses the same turn rule.
- The slot-wait re-take passed new=not out in our branch; here it is a separate `unadmitted` flag, so it stands
  back for an image like a new request but STRATA_ADMIT_SHORT_FIRST does not order it (upstream's ordering is
  unchanged) and load_counts still classifies it by upstream's `new` field.
- A STRATA_COALESCE_PREFILL follower that holds a preslot never stands back (the image would wait for its slot).
- _generate_alone follows upstream's solo path: logprob lines on the request, queue deadline and
  _strata_queue_started, _control/_drain_control on the request's own lines_q (#4451), and _quarantine_control
  when the engine does not confirm the STOP; _take_engine_alone also honours the queue deadline. It notes
  "alone" for STRATA_PREFIX_DIAG. restart() forgets mrope_slots (77e9b9e1).
- Vision start: upstream's elastic encoder (_vision_up) is kept; _vision_start (a dead non-elastic encoder) runs
  before it on the image paths; prepare() skips both when every picture is cached; the tool-picture path keeps
  upstream's RuntimeError catch (EngineDied is one). The par ensure_loaded keeps upstream's _inference_fifo and
  its queued_counted bookkeeping instead of our try/except.
- serve/test_image_alone.py: production's version (77e9b9e1 cases included: the handshake, slot tables over HTTP);
  the engine-without-process helper gets upstream's arrivals and lines.
- docs/DETAILS.md: "Pictures and parallel requests" (from f2ef22b3, without STRATA_IMAGE_HISTORY, which is
  dropped, and without the engine's STRATA_MROPE_SLOTS, not ported yet) and the image_alone field of GET /v1/load.

