+### Pictures and parallel requests (`"parallel"`, `--batch`)
+
+With several batch slots the engine keeps one M-RoPE position table per GPU, which every slot reads, so an image request
+next to other slots would mix its picture's positions into their rows. The server therefore runs an image request
+**alone**: from its arrival no new request is admitted, the slots that decode finish, then it runs on the solo path, and
+image requests queue one after another. `STRATA_IMAGE_WAIT_S` (default 120 s, 0 = no limit) is how long it waits for the
+slots; after that it gets a 503 the client can retry, and the requests held behind it go on. An engine that says
+`INFO ... mrope_slots=1` keeps one table region per slot; the server then admits image requests into slots like text
+ones. A vision encoder that died or cannot start fails only requests with images; text requests go on without it.
+
